  "title": "Index vs length",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## A list of directions\n\n`const dirs = [\"east\", \"east\", \"south\"]`. Index `0` is the first item. `dirs.length` is `3`. The last item is at `length - 1`, not `length`."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "last-index",
      "promptMd": "For `[\"east\", \"south\"]`, the last index is…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "2",
          "md": "`2` — same as length",
          "misconceptionId": "off-by-one-inclusive"
        },
        {
          "id": "1",
          "md": "`1` — length minus one"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "1"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "walk-dirs",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> Walk every string in `dirs` with `Player.move`. Do not hard-code four moves.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "files/main.js",
          "role": "edit"
        },
        {
          "path": "files/hidden.test.js",
          "role": "hidden-test"
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "js-assert"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "The list already holds the route. The starter ignores it and moves once by hand."
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "Walk the list itself, so adding a direction to `dirs` changes the path with no other edit."
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "`for (const dir of dirs) { … }` hands you each string in turn."
        },
        {
          "level": 4,
          "kind": "assist",
          "md": "const dirs = [\"east\", \"east\", \"south\"]\nfor (const dir of dirs) Player.move(dir)\nmodule.exports = { dirs }"
        }
